---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';const p='/equipment/10-03/',man='https://moldevkb.blob.core.windows.net/kb01/documents/cns/axopatch-200b-userguide-2500-121e.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Axopatch 200B electronic level witness" subtitle="" wide={true} description="Measure an inert switched-resistor level through an ideal Axopatch scaled-output chain."><script is:inline>window.axLevels=import('/equipment/10-03/levels.mjs');</script><article class="equipment" id="axopatch"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/10-03/">← Equipment 10-03</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#ax-ref">References</a><a href="#ax-proof">Verification</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">10-03 / LOW-CURRENT ELECTRONICS</p><h2>Six picoamps through the output chain</h2><p class="eq-lede">Switch a passive electronic resistor from disconnected to connected and back. At 0.1 nS and 60 mV, the settled current moves by 6 pA. Check how the low-pass setting changes the edge without changing its settled value.</p></header>
<div class="cols"><section><p class="eq-meta">01 / RACK AND HEADSTAGE</p><h3>Axopatch 200B · CV203BU</h3><div id="ax-view" aria-label="Interactive Axopatch 200B rack and inert switched-resistor headstage fixture"></div><small id="ax-model" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</small><div class="tools"><button id="ax-front">Rack front</button><button id="ax-head">Electronic fixture</button><button id="ax-rear">Rear I/O</button></div><p>Drag to orbit or zoom. Select gain, filter, power, meter or dummy fixture in the model, or use the electronic bench controls. Other front-panel controls are visual references only.</p></section>
<section><p class="eq-meta">02 / ELECTRONIC FIXTURE</p><h3>Closed, conducting, closed</h3><div class="fields"><label>Conducting level (nS)<input id="ax-conductanceNS" type="number" min="0" max="4" step="any" value=".1"/></label><label>Signed drive (mV)<input id="ax-biasMV" type="number" min="-100" max="100" step="any" value="60"/></label><label>Output gain α<select id="ax-gain">{[.5,1,2,5,10,20,50,100,200,500].map(x=><option value={x} selected={x===20}>{x} ×</option>)}</select></label><label>Ideal Bessel cutoff<select id="ax-fcHz">{[1,2,5,10].map(x=><option value={1000*x}>{x} kHz</option>)}</select></label></div><div class="tools"><button class="run" id="ax-run">Acquire trace</button><button id="ax-connect">Disconnect dummy</button><button id="ax-power">Disable amplifier</button><button id="ax-reset">Reset example</button></div><p id="ax-status" role="status"></p></section></div>
<section><p class="eq-meta">03 / READOUT</p><h3>Ideal step versus amplifier output</h3><p id="ax-result" aria-live="polite"></p><canvas id="ax-plot" width="620" height="245" aria-label="Electronic conducting step and four pole filtered current"></canvas><p>Teal: unfiltered electrical source. Gold: filtered current referred back to the input. The SCALED OUTPUT uses the documented αβ mV/pA convention. Export contains volts for scope/digitizer exchange.</p><div class="tools"><button id="ax-json" disabled>Export acquisition JSON</button><button id="ax-wave" disabled>Export voltage waveform</button><a href={p+'primary-example.json'} download>Example waveform</a></div></section>
<section id="ax-ref"><p class="eq-meta">04 / REFERENCE</p><h3>One documented hardware configuration</h3><p><a href={man+'#page=132'}>Axon manufacturer manual, printed p. 116</a> gives 19 × 3.5 × 12.5 in rack dimensions, excluding modeled protrusions, and CV203BU case 0.7 × 0.75 × 4.2 in. The <a href="https://www.eastport.cz/images/produkty/AxoPatch-200B.jpg">front oblique equipment photograph</a> informs the blue case, handles, engraved groups and headstage. Front/rear placement, short harness, connectors and electronic resistor box are original estimates. The fixture is not a proprietary model cell.</p><p>The <a href={man+'#page=130'}>manufacturer specifications, pp. 113–114</a> identify SCALED OUTPUT I in voltage-clamp representation, gain αβ and a four-pole Bessel output with 1, 2, 5, 10 and 100 kHz marked settings. The selected β=1 electronic representation supports only 1–10 kHz here. No functional settings for living preparations, thermal compensation or real apparatus control.</p><div class="tools"><a href={p+'build-model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a><a href={p+'axopatch-200b.glb'} download>Download GLB</a><a href={p+'xr.json'}>Geometry and VR targets</a><a href={p+'levels.mjs'}>Solver and actions</a></div></section>
<section id="ax-proof"><p class="eq-meta">05 / METHOD &amp; VERIFICATION</p><h3>Analytic current and bandwidth</h3><p>The zero/one electronic conductance gate is high from 5 to 15 ms; I=GV. At the documented α gain and β=1 mV/pA, 6 pA at α=20 gives 120 mV. The analytic step response is formed from residues of H(s)=105/(s⁴+10s³+45s²+105s+105), scaled so the cutoff is −3.0103 dB. Rise and fall are shifted copies of that response with opposite signs. The ideal equivalent noise bandwidth is ∫|H(f)|²df (computed to 40× cutoff); the displayed signal itself has no added noise.</p><p><b>Independent targets:</b> +6 pA at default, ±10⁻⁵ pA; +0.120 V, ±10⁻⁷ V; cutoff −3.01029996 dB, 10⁻⁹ dB; higher cutoff gives faster arrival. The model rejects loss of virtual connection and ±10 V model overrange. Samples are 100 kS/s over 22 ms. Clamp dynamics, capacitance, offsets, reset intervals, lead loading and hardware noise are not modeled. Numerical verification is not calibration of the physical device.</p><p><code>bts.axopatch-levels.v1</code> contains synthetic state, input-referred current in A and output in V, dt in seconds and contact/sample IDs. The <code>bts.analog-waveform.v1</code> export can be imported in the <a href="/simulations/equipment/09-04/simulator/">oscilloscope</a> or <a href="/simulations/equipment/10-02/simulator/">digitizer</a>. <a href={p+'handoff.json'}>Verified replay report</a>. Geometry is VR-ready with stable anchors; no physical headset test is claimed.</p></section>
</article></Layout><script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/10-03/client.mjs';</script><style is:global>
#axopatch .cols,#axopatch .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.13fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:.8rem}#axopatch section{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1rem;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}#axopatch .cols section{margin:0}#axopatch .eq-meta{margin:0}#axopatch h3{margin:.3rem 0 .6rem;font-size:1.5rem}#axopatch .tools{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.44rem;margin:.64rem 0}#axopatch label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0}#axopatch button,#axopatch input,#axopatch select{min-height:40px;padding:.37rem;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;font:inherit;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--panel,transparent);color:var(--text)}#axopatch button{cursor:pointer}#axopatch button.run{color:white;background:#355d57}#axopatch button:disabled{opacity:.5}#ax-view{height:clamp(267px,31vw,410px);background:#27353a}#ax-view canvas{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;touch-action:none}#ax-plot{width:min(100%,755px);height:auto;display:block}#ax-result{font-weight:bold}@media(max-width:760px){#axopatch .cols{grid-template-columns:1fr}#axopatch section{padding:.68rem}}
</style>
